  "text_sample": "Your Page Title aubergine projects menu aubergine close Services Projects Garden care About Areas Journal Free quote Overview +34 960 000 000 [email protected] Cam\u00ed de Vera 18, 46022 Valencia 9 April 2026 Drip lines, explained How we size an irrigation system, where the water goes, and the controller settings for each season. Written by Matteo Bassi Topic Water Reading 1 min Sprinklers throw water into the air, onto paths and walls, and lose a third of it to the wind before it reaches a root. A drip line puts it on the soil, slowly, where the roots are. In a Mediterranean garden that is the difference between a bill and a much smaller bill. How a system is laid out We split every garden into zones by what the plants need. Lawns, new planting, established shrubs and trees each get their own valve, because a ten year old olive and a bed planted last week should never share a schedule. Each zone gets a line with emitters every 30 cm, pressure compensated so the last plant gets as much as the first. Trees get a ring of line around the drip edge of the canopy, not against the trunk. How much water For new planting, little and often until the roots are established: twenty minutes every o",
